{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1463, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given a length-N sequence A=(A_1,A_2,\\ldots,A_N) of positive integers.\nDetermine whether A is a geometric progression.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN\r\nA_1 A_2 \\ldots A_N\n\nOutput\n\nIf A is a geometric progression, print Yes; otherwise, print No.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 2 \\leq N \\leq 100\n- 1 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^9\n- All input values are integers.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n5\r\n3 6 12 24 48\n\nSample Output 1\n\nYes\r\n\nA=(3,6,12,24,48).\nA is a geometric progression with first term 3, common ratio 2, and five terms.\r\nTherefore, print Yes.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n3\r\n1 2 3\n\nSample Output 2\n\nNo\r\n\nA=(1,2,3).\r\nSince A_1 : A_2 = 1 : 2 \\neq 2 : 3 = A_2 : A_3, A is not a geometric progression.\r\nTherefore, print No.\n\nSample Input 3\n\n2\r\n10 8\n\nSample Output 3\n\nYes\r\n\nA is a geometric progression with first term 10, common ratio 0.8, and two terms.\r\nTherefore, print Yes.\n\n### Format: Read the inputs from stdin solve the problem and write the answer to stdout (do not directly test on the sample inputs). Enclose your code within delimiters as follows. Ensure that when the python program runs, it reads the inputs, runs the algorithm and writes output to STDOUT.\n```python\n# YOUR CODE HERE\n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1508, "char_start": 1475, "quote": "Input:\n5\n3 6 12 24 48\nOutput:\nYes", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1545, "char_start": 1520, "quote": "Input:\n3\n1 2 3\nOutput:\nNo", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R5", "source": {"char_end": 1582, "char_start": 1557, "quote": "Input:\n2\n10 8\nOutput:\nYes", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 3: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "5c7b3c7ae329e283bf3bdf10872ba1249506033a9178f17856b77a3d63bf0a42", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "82fca56317d747b6da7cd078d43ede339a90737dbc4f4f01722b4ac9ed14a792", "seq": 2}
